<PolicyLayout title="Cookie policy" description="Your choices for essential storage and optional Google Analytics on the BlogStack website.">
<h2>Essential preferences</h2><p>We store your cookie choice in your browser so you do not have to choose on every page. The preference expires after 180 days. If browser storage is unavailable or you clear it, we ask again. Authentication storage in the publishing dashboard is separate and is needed to sign in.</p>
<h2>Optional Google Analytics</h2><p>With your permission, this marketing website loads Google Analytics 4 to understand page visits and navigation. Google Analytics may set first-party cookies such as <code>_ga</code> and <code>_ga_*</code>. We configure a 180-day cookie lifetime and do not enable advertising personalization or Google signals.</p><p>The Google Analytics tag is blocked until you accept analytics. The site also respects Do Not Track and Global Privacy Control. We send page locations without query strings or fragments and reduce referrers to their origin; we do not send setup form values, account details or article drafts to Google Analytics.</p>
<h2>Change your choice</h2><p>Use <button type="button" data-cookie-settings>Cookie preferences</button> here or in the footer. Choosing Essential only turns analytics off, removes the site's Google Analytics cookies where accessible, and reloads the page without the tag. Your choice does not affect your ability to browse the site.</p>
<h2>Analytics on blogs built with BlogStack</h2><p>The optional reader analytics in the BlogStack product is a separate system. It measures article views and link clicks through Cloudflare Analytics Engine without setting analytics cookies. A website owner chooses whether to enable that integration. See the <a href="/privacy">privacy policy</a> for the information each system handles.</p>
<h2>More information</h2><p>Read <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy">Google's privacy policy</a> and <a href="https://support.google.com/analytics/answer/6004245">Google Analytics data practices</a> for Google's processing. Contact us using the address below with questions about your choices.</p>
</PolicyLayout>
